# -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Context Types 
# In OpenREL, Context Types are used to unambigously identify context options and scenarios applicable to agents
# The Context Types are typically used to define prohibitions.
# -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

# context
@base <http://www.w3.org/ns/openrel/0/> .
@prefix : <http://www.w3.org/ns/openrel/0/> . 
# RDF-related
@prefix rdf: <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix skos: <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#> .
@prefix owl: <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .
# general content
@prefix schema: <http://schema.org/> .
@prefix foaf: <http://xmlns.com/foaf/0.1/> .
@prefix vcard: <http://www.w3.org/2006/vcard/ns#> .
# rdmi-related
@prefix dct: <http://purl.org/dc/terms/> .
@prefix dcat: <http://www.w3.org/ns/dcat#> .
@prefix dcatap: <http://data.europa.eu/r5r/> .
@prefix r3d: <https://schema.re3data.org/4-0/re3dataV4-0.xsd> .
@prefix coar: <http://purl.org/coar/> .
# rights-related
@prefix odrl: <http://www.w3.org/ns/odrl/2/> .
@prefix cc: <http://creativecommons.org/ns#> .
